# NOTICE — provenance and vendored source

This file is required by [ADR 0008](./docs/adr/0008-identity-licensing-vendoring.md)
before any vendored source is committed.

## Upstream project

- Project: [AuthMeReloaded](https://github.com/AuthMe/AuthMeReloaded)
- Licence: GPL-3.0
- Exact commit vendored from: `56e9a66b`

The vendored file below is a self-contained public-domain BCrypt implementation
(jBCrypt 0.4, Damien Miller, ISC), vendored because AuthMe's own BCrypt wrappers
at `56e9a66b` delegate to BouncyCastle, which login-core does not ship.

## Vendored files

- `src/main/java/com/hizeric/logincore/authme/BCrypt.java` — self-contained BCrypt
  implementation vendored from jBCrypt 0.4 (Damien Miller, ISC-style licence),
  upstream path `src/main/java/org/mindrot/BCrypt.java` at
  https://github.com/jeremyh/jBCrypt (tree `e015c2c`); upstream copyright header
  retained verbatim. Package renamed and `hashpw` widened to accept `$2b$`/`$2y$`.
  AuthMeReloaded commit `56e9a66b` is the behavioural reference for those prefixes:
  `authme-core/src/main/java/fr/xephi/authme/security/crypts/BCrypt.java` and
  `authme-core/src/main/java/fr/xephi/authme/security/crypts/BCrypt2y.java`.
  Those upstream classes delegate to BouncyCastle `OpenBSDBCrypt`, which would
  require a new Gradle dependency, so the public-domain algorithm was vendored
  instead.

Local file using the vendored source (not itself vendored):
`src/main/java/com/hizeric/logincore/authme/AuthMePasswords.java`.

When a file is vendored, retain its upstream copyright and licence headers
